criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
Age: women ≥ 70 years, men ≥ 75 years;
Indication for a primary, unilateral, cementless total hip arthroplasty;
Stable gait without assistive devices preoperatively;
Written informed consent
Exclusion criteria:
Age: women < 70 years, men < 75 years;
BMI > 40;
Concomitant rheumatological or neurological conditions affecting gait;
Revision hip surgery;
Inability to give informed consent
